🚀 QuantPy Control Panel | Local Setup Guide
This guide will help you set up and run the QuantPy Trading Dashboard on your local machine. This version includes secure backend authentication, 2FA (TOTP), and AI-powered analysis.

Prerequisites
Before you begin, ensure you have Python 3.8+ installed on your system.
Step 1: Installation
Clone or move into your project directory and install the required dependencies:

Bash
pip install flask flask-session python-dotenv pyotp bcrypt qrcode[pil] yfinance anthropic pandas numpy
Step 2: Configure Environment Variables
Create a file named .env in the root directory (the same folder as server.py). Add the following content and replace the placeholders with your actual data:

Code-Snippet
# API Key for AI Analysis
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_sk_ant_key_here

# Security - Generate a random string for sessions
# You can use: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
SECRET_KEY=XYZ

# User Credentials
QUANT_USER=USERNAME
QUANT_PASSWORD=your_secure_password_here
[!IMPORTANT]
Never share your .env file or commit it to GitHub. Add .env to your .gitignore file.

📱 Step 3: Setup 2FA (Two-Factor Authentication)
Before starting the server for the first time, you must set up your Authenticator App:

Run the setup script:

Bash
python setup_2fa.py
A QR code will be generated and saved in the .secrets/ folder as a .png file.

Open the image and scan it with Google Authenticator, Authy, or Microsoft Authenticator.

Enter the 6-digit code in the terminal to verify the setup.

🚀 Step 4: Start the Server
Once 2FA is configured, you can launch the dashboard:

Bash
python server.py
URL: [http://IP](http://IP)

Login: Use the credentials defined in your .env file.

2FA: Enter the rotating 6-digit code from your phone app.

